 ("What is the Jarisch–Herxheimer reaction?", ["Acute febrile reaction within 2–24 h of first antibiotic dose (penicillin) for spirochaetal infection — fever, chills, myalgia, headache, worsening rash, hypotension — due to release of treponemal lipoproteins/ cytokines; common in secondary syphilis; treat with antipyretics, reassurance; in pregnancy may cause preterm labour/ fetal distress (monitor); not an allergy — continue treatment"]),
