 ("What is genital LS–LP overlap and differentiation?", ["LP: erosive, involves vagina (LS spares vagina), Wickham's striae at margins, oral involvement; LS: porcelain-white atrophy, figure-of-eight, perianal; overlap occurs — biopsy helps; both treated with clobetasol"]),
