dict(case="Parry–Romberg syndrome", qa=[
 ("What is the pathogenesis?", ["Not fully known — considered an autoimmune localised scleroderma variant (linear morphoea spectrum); other theories: sympathetic nervous system dysfunction, trigeminal neuritis, infection (Borrelia), trauma; histology of skin shows sclerosis/ atrophy with perivascular lymphocytes"]),
 ("Histopathology findings.", ["Early: perivascular and periadnexal lymphocytic infiltrate in dermis/ subcutis; late: dermal sclerosis or simply atrophy of dermis and subcutaneous fat with loss of adnexa, sometimes muscle atrophy; similar to linear morphoea"]),
 ("What is the role of autologous fat grafting?", ["Lipofilling (Coleman technique — harvesting fat by liposuction, purification by centrifugation, micro-injection in layers) restores volume once disease is inactive; may need multiple sessions; some evidence of improved skin quality from adipose stem cells; complications — resorption, cysts, asymmetry"]),
 ("How is disease inactivity determined before reconstruction?", ["Stable facial measurements and photographs for ≥1–2 years, no new symptoms, MRI without active inflammation, off systemic therapy or on stable dose — then reconstructive surgery"]),
 ("Prognosis for neurological involvement.", ["Seizures may persist and need long-term antiepileptics; brain lesions often stable; rarely progressive neurological deficits; neurological involvement can predate skin changes"]),
 ("Classify facial hemiatrophy by severity (Guerrero-Santos).", ["Type I: skin and subcutaneous tissue (mild); II: plus muscle; III: plus cartilage/ bone — moderate; IV: severe with skeletal deformity — guides reconstructive planning"]),
 ]),
