 ("What is hypertrophic (verrucous) DLE?", ["Thick hyperkeratotic warty plaques on extensor arms/ face — resembles SCC, keratoacanthoma, hypertrophic LP; histology shows interface changes with marked hyperkeratosis; responds to acitretin/ isotretinoin, intralesional steroids, thalidomide"]),
 ("Antimalarial dosing and combination.", ["HCQ ≤5 mg/kg real body weight/day; chloroquine ≤2.3 mg/kg/day; never combine HCQ and chloroquine (retinal toxicity); add quinacrine 100 mg/day to either for refractory disease (quinacrine causes yellow skin, rarely aplastic anaemia, no retinopathy); response takes 6–12 weeks"]),
